From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] scsi: ufs: qcom: do not enable the lane clocks twice

ufs_qcom_enable_lane_clks() lost its is_lane_clks_enabled check when it moved
to clk_bulk (the bulk covers every clock of the UFS node, ref_clk included),
but its callers overlap. After a system suspend at spm_lvl 3 (link hibern8),
ufshcd_setup_clocks(on) PRE_CHANGE enables the bulk because the link is in
hibern8, then ufs_qcom_resume() enables it again, while the suspend path
disabled it once. Every resume leaks one enable of every UFS clock.

Evidence on ROG5 (r31, 2026-09-26, 16 successful suspends): clk_summary shows
gcc_ufs_phy_axi_clk, unipro_core, ahb, the three symbol clocks at
enable/prepare count 16 while UFS is clock-gated (18 while ungated), and
bi_tcxo at 22, 16 of them from 1d84000.ufshc ref_clk. So UFS clock gating no
longer gates anything, GPLL0 stays on, and the XO (bi_tcxo is the non-AO
RPMh XO vote, which covers the sleep set) is held through suspend and idle.

Make the enable idempotent, matching ufs_qcom_disable_lane_clks().

--- a/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c
@@ -356,6 +356,16 @@
 {
 	int err;
 
+	/*
+	 * Callers overlap: after a hibern8 system suspend, setup_clocks(on)
+	 * PRE_CHANGE enables the clocks and ufs_qcom_resume() enables them
+	 * again, while suspend disables them once. Keep this idempotent like
+	 * ufs_qcom_disable_lane_clks(), or every resume leaks one enable of
+	 * every UFS clock (bi_tcxo included) and clock gating stops working.
+	 */
+	if (host->is_lane_clks_enabled)
+		return 0;
+
 	err = clk_bulk_prepare_enable(host->num_clks, host->clks);
 	if (err)
 		return err;
